{"schemaVersion":1,"systemCode":"BGN-PCGN:cv-Cyrl:Latn:2011","dependencies":[],"metadata":{"authority_id":"bgnpcgn","id":"2011","language":"iso-639-1:cv","source_script":"Cyrl","destination_script":"Latn","name":"Romanization of Chuvash (BGN/PCGN 2011 System)","url":"https://geonames.nga.mil/gns/html/Romanization/ROMANIZATION%20OF%20CHUVASH.pdf","creation_date":"2011","confirmation_date":"2017-10","description":"The BGN/PCGN system for Chuvash is designed for use in romanizing names written\n    in the Chuvash Cyrillic alphabet. Chuvash is an official language within Chuvashiya, one of\n    the republics of the Russian Federation.","notes":["The character e should be romanized ye initially, after the vowel characters a, e, ё, и, о, у, ы, э, ю, and я, and after й, ъ, and ь. In all other instances, it should be romanized e.","The character ё should be romanized yë initially, after the vowel characters a, e, ё, и, о, у, ы, э, ю, and я, and after й, ъ, and ь. In all other instances, it should be romanized ё. Often the dieresis is not shown in Cyrillic, and in this case, the character should be romanized as ‘ë’/‘yë’, as outlined above, if known to be relevant, or otherwise ‘e’/‘ye’ as described in note 1.","An inventory of letter-diacritic combinations, with their Unicode encoding, in addition to the unmodified letters of the basic Roman script is:\n\nĂ (U+0102) ă (U+0103)\nË (U+00CB) ë (U+00EB)\nĔ (U+0114) ĕ (U+0115)\nŚ (U+015A) ś (U+015B)\nÜ (U+00DC) ü (U+00FC)\nĖ (U+0116) ė (U+0117)","The Romanization columns show only lowercase forms but, when romanizing, uppercase and lowercase Roman letters as appropriate should be used.","The source table renders the Cyrillic letter ҫ (U+04AA, U+04AB) with the glyphs of Latin ç (U+00C7, U+00E7); this implementation maps from the Cyrillic codepoints."]},"stages":[{"kind":"stage","name":"main","rules":[{"kind":"sub","from":{"kind":"string","value":"Е"},"to":{"kind":"string","value":"YЕ"},"before":{"kind":"alias","name":"cv_extvowel"